        "original_id": "c57f4177-5c18-5e45-b592-1806943de7bc",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Plants: Geissorhiza, Geissorhiza radians, Stenocarpus\n- Places: Northern Cape, South Africa, Sandlane, Mbabane\n- Families: iris family, Proteaceae\n\nFacts:\n- In 1803, Geissorhiza was first described as a genus.\n- Geissorhiza is a genus of about 80 species of deciduous perennial flowering plants in the iris family.\n- Stenocarpus is a genus of about 25 known species of woody trees or shrubs in the plant family Proteaceae.\n- Geissorhiza radians is a species in the genus Geissorhiza.\n- Geissorhiza radians grows in Northern Cape, South Africa.\n- Sandlane is located near the border with South Africa.\n- Sandlane is 40 kilometres southwest of Mbabane.",
